		{
			dependencies: ["44EA000000000004"]
			description: [
				"The &eMillstone&r grinds slowly but surely - gravel to flint, bones to meal, wheat to flour. Your first powered processing block, and it never asks for a coffee break."
				""
				"&e&lWhy start here and not with Crushing Wheels.&r The Millstone is one block, costs almost no stress, and takes rotation from any direction. Crushing Wheels are a two-block multiblock that needs them counter-rotating at matched speed and eats far more SU. The Millstone gets you grinding &lnow&r; upgrade when your water wheels can afford it."
				""
				"&7Feed it from the top with a funnel or hopper; it drops output out the bottom. Put a hopper underneath and a chest below that and it runs unattended.&r"
				""
				"&e&lWhat it is actually for in this pack:&r &7cobblestone &8→&7 gravel &8→&7 sand&r without hammering. That is your entire sieve chain, automated, using a block you can afford in your first hour with Create."
				""
				"&8It is slow. That is fine - it is slow while you are asleep."
			]
			icon: "create:millstone"
			id: "44EA000000000007"
			rewards: [{
				count: 8
				id: "44EA000000000107"
				item: "minecraft:bone_meal"
				type: "item"
			}]
			subtitle: "&7Grind it out"
			tasks: [{
				id: "44EA000000000207"
				item: "create:millstone"
				type: "item"
			}]
			title: "&2The Millstone"
			x: -2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["44EA000000000006"]
			description: [
				"An &eEncased Fan&r behind water becomes a &ewashing line&r: bulk-wash &egravel into iron and copper nuggets&r, sand into clay, soul sand into gold."
				""
				"This is the Kinetic Age's answer to the sieve - park a chest, walk away, come back rich."
